/**
 * @defgroup StgmGeo StgmGeo — Small-strip Thin-Gap Chamber Geometry
 * @ingroup StarVMCGeometry
 * @brief AGML geometry definition for the STAR small-strip Thin-Gap Chamber (sTGC),
 *        detector tag STGM.
 *
 * @details
 * The small-strip Thin-Gap Chamber (sTGC) is a four-station gaseous tracking detector
 * designed for the STAR Forward Detector Upgrade (FWD), targeting the BES-II physics
 * programme.  It provides charged-particle tracking at far-forward pseudorapidities in
 * conjunction with the Forward Silicon Tracker (FST).
 *
 * **Physical layout:**
 * The sTGC mother volume STGM is placed in the STAR cave at z = 338.84 cm (with a +5.9 cm
 * y-offset for the STAR global tilt) and subtends a z half-length of 30 cm.  Four stations
 * are located at z offsets −26.50, −8.89, +8.80, and +26.58 cm, placing them physically at
 * z ≈ 312, 330, 348, and 365 cm from the IP.  Each station consists of four pentagon-shaped
 * detector modules (STFM) arranged with 90° rotational symmetry, covering an acceptance from
 * r ≈ 2.25 cm to r ≈ 32.5 cm.
 *
 * **Module structure:**
 * Each STFM pentagon module is built from three sub-assemblies:
 *   - STMP — G10 PCB layer (half-thickness 1.59 mm), decomposed into three sub-shapes
 *     (polygon + two boxes: STPP, STPL, STPS).
 *   - STMG — gas active volume (NPCO2, half-depth 3.19 mm); sensitive detector medium;
 *     decomposed into STGP, STGL, STGS.
 *   - STMH — aluminium honeycomb structural layer (half-depth 5.31 mm);
 *     decomposed into STHP, STHL, STHS.
 *
 * Per-module misalignment corrections are read from the alignment tables
 * @c Geometry/stgc/pentOnStation and @c Geometry/stgc/stationOnStgc.
 *
 * **Combined Si+sTGC mode:**
 * The MAIN structure carries a `zsi(7)` array (93.3, 140.0, 186.6, 280.9, 303.7,
 * 326.6, 349.4 cm) for placing additional silicon discs alongside the sTGC stations in the
 * combined FWD configuration activated by setup tag @c STGCv1.
 *
 * @par Author
 * Daniel Brandenburg
 *
 * @par Created
 * 19 August 2021
 *
 * @{
 */

/**
 * @defgroup StgmGeoDefault StgmGeo1 — Default sTGC Four-Station Geometry
 * @ingroup StgmGeo
 * @brief Four sTGC stations at z ≈ 312, 330, 348, 365 cm with full misalignment support.
 *
 * @details Activated by setup tag @c STGCon (MAIN.version = 3.0).  All four stations are
 * enabled.  Front-end electronics (TFEE) and mechanical support brackets (BRAC: corner,
 * middle, edge, and coax connector) are included in the volume description.
 */

/**
 * @defgroup StgmGeoFWD StgmGeo1 — Combined Si+sTGC FWD Configuration
 * @ingroup StgmGeo
 * @brief sTGC stations plus seven silicon disc positions for the full Forward Detector system.
 *
 * @details Activated by setup tag @c STGCv1 (MAIN.version = 3.0, type = 1, useids = 0,
 * active = {0,…,0}).  Silicon disc z-positions from MAIN.zsi = {93.3, 140.0, 186.6,
 * 280.9, 303.7, 326.6, 349.4} cm, together with four sTGC stations, form the complete
 * Forward Detector as envisioned for BES-II running.
 */

/**
 * @}
 */
